# Vercel Speed Insights Installation Report

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for the Orienta Next.js project following the latest official documentation from Vercel.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- **Added dependency**: `@vercel/speed-insights` version `^2.0.0`
- **Files modified**: 
  - `package.json` - Added @vercel/speed-insights to dependencies
  - `package-lock.json` - Updated with new dependency and its sub-dependencies

### 2. Component Integration
- **File modified**: `src/app/layout.tsx`
- **Changes**:
  - Added import statement: `import { SpeedInsights } from "@vercel/speed-insights/next";`
  - Added `<SpeedInsights />` component at the end of the `<body>` tag
  - The component is placed after existing components (BottomNav, ServiceWorkerRegister) to avoid interference with app functionality

## Implementation Details

### Framework Detection
- Identified the project as **Next.js 16.4.0** with App Router
- Used the appropriate Next.js-specific import path: `@vercel/speed-insights/next`

### Documentation Source
- Fetched latest installation instructions from: https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart
- Followed official Vercel guidelines for Next.js App Router integration

### Code Location
The SpeedInsights component was added to the root layout file (`src/app/layout.tsx`), which wraps the entire application. This ensures Speed Insights tracking is active across all pages.

## Verification Steps Completed

✅ **Linting**: Ran ESLint on modified file - no errors introduced
✅ **Build**: Successfully built the project with `npm run build`
✅ **Tests**: All 468 tests pass in 21 test suites
✅ **Type Checking**: Layout file has no TypeScript errors related to our changes

## Next Steps for Activation

After deployment to Vercel:
1. The tracking script will automatically be available at `/_vercel/speed-insights/*`
2. Data collection begins immediately
3. Metrics will be visible in the Vercel Dashboard under the Speed Insights section after users visit the site
4. It may take several days of traffic to accumulate meaningful data

## Technical Notes

- The SpeedInsights component is a zero-config implementation that automatically collects Web Vitals
- No additional configuration is required for basic functionality
- The component works seamlessly with Next.js Server Components and App Router
- Installation was done with `--ignore-scripts` flag to bypass build issues with better-sqlite3 native module
